# The org's base .gitignore -- the secret paths every TCOS repo excludes.
#
# This lives here because .github is where org-wide GitHub administration
# belongs. Note the real limit: GitHub inherits community health files from
# this repo (CODE_OF_CONDUCT, CONTRIBUTING, the fallback CODEOWNERS) but it
# does NOT inherit .gitignore. Nothing propagates this on its own. It is
# synced by `hee check gitignore --fix`, which splices it into a repo between
# markers so a later run replaces the block instead of appending a second one.
#
# Why it exists, 2026-09-06: a GPG-sealed pve admin credential was committed
# to the public human-execution-engine repo inside a documentation typo PR.
# The ignore rule that allowed it was `!.hee/secrets/*.gpg`, copied from
# fleet-ops -- where it is correct, because that repo is private and really
# does track 7 sealed files. In the public repo it had protected zero files.
# The force-push did not undo it: the commit and blob are still served by
# SHA. See fleet-ops#410.
#
# Deliberately narrow. A baseline that matches too much gets negated back by
# whoever it inconveniences, and a negation is exactly what published that
# credential.
#
# NEVER add a negation that re-includes one of these in a public repo.

secrets/
.hee/secrets/
*.env
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
.netrc
id_rsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
